<%
  var b = company.business;
  var d = shippingCfg.DISPATCH;
%>

<div class="container ship-page" style="padding-top:1.25rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem">
  <nav class="col-page__breadcrumb" style="margin-bottom:1.75rem" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="<%= marketPath('/') %>">Home</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    <span aria-current="page">Shipping &amp; Delivery</span>
  </nav>

  <p class="label-overline" style="margin-bottom:0.9rem">Customer information</p>
  <h1 class="ship-page__title">Shipping &amp; Delivery</h1>
  <p class="ship-page__lede">
    Everything on this page is what the checkout actually does and what we
    declare to Google. There is one shipping policy and this is it.
  </p>

  <div class="ship-banner">
    <p class="ship-banner__head"><%= shippingCfg.copy.short %></p>
    <p class="ship-banner__sub">
      Every order ships tracked, at our cost, wherever you are. No minimum spend,
      no threshold to reach, and no cheaper untracked option to decline.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>How long it takes</h2>

  <%/* Rendered from config/shipping.js rather than written out by hand.
       The old version of this table lived in a database page as literal
       HTML while the Offer schema quoted a single flat US rate to every
       shopper on earth and the announcement bar quoted a third figure —
       three different answers to "what will delivery cost me", which is
       the "shipping mismatch" a Merchant Center reviewer catches by
       comparing the feed against this page. Now there is one source. */%>
  <div class="legal-table-wrap">
    <table class="legal-table">
      <caption class="sr-only">Carriers, delivery estimates and cost by destination. Shipping is free to every destination listed.</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Destination</th>
          <th scope="col">Carrier</th>
          <th scope="col">Estimated delivery</th>
          <th scope="col">Cost</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <% shippingCfg.REGIONS.forEach(function (r) { %>
          <tr>
            <th scope="row"><%= r.name %></th>
            <td><%= r.carrier %></td>
            <td><%= r.transitDays[0] %>&ndash;<%= r.transitDays[1] %> business days</td>
            <td class="ship-free">Free</td>
          </tr>
        <% }); %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Delivery estimates are counted from dispatch, not from when you order, and they
    are the carrier's estimate rather than a guarantee. All prices are in
    <%= b.currency %>.
  </p>

  <h2>When your order leaves us</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      In-stock orders placed before <%= d.cutoffLocal %> <%= d.cutoffTimezone %> on a business day
      are dispatched the same day. After that, or at a weekend or public holiday,
      they go the next business day.
    </li>
    <li>
      Preorders ship on the publisher's release date, or within
      <%= d.preorderBusinessDaysAfterRelease %> business days of it. You are charged when you
      place the preorder, not on release day. See the full
      <a href="<%= marketPath('/collection/preorders') %>">preorder terms</a> on any preorder listing.
    </li>
    <li>
      You get a tracking number by email the moment the label is created.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tracking and cover</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every order ships tracked, with no exceptions and no cheaper untracked option.</li>
    <li>Every order is covered against loss or damage in transit. If it arrives damaged or does not arrive, that is our problem to fix, not yours to absorb.</li>
    <li>Orders over $<%= shippingCfg.SIGNATURE_REQUIRED_OVER_USD %> require a signature on delivery.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we pack</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Booster boxes and elite trainer boxes are individually wrapped before they go in the outer carton.</li>
    <li>Everything ships in a rigid corrugated box sized so the contents cannot move. Corners and seals are what a collector inspects first, so they are what the packaging is designed to protect.</li>
    <li>Master cases ship in the distributor's own sealed shipper, unopened.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>International orders, duties and taxes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Import duty, VAT and customs handling fees are set by the destination country,
      are charged to you by the carrier or the customs authority, and are
      <strong>not</strong> included in the price you pay us.
    </li>
    <li>
      We declare the true value of every shipment. We do not mark orders as gifts and
      we do not undervalue them. Being asked to is the one request we always refuse:
      it is customs fraud, and it is the buyer who carries the consequence.
    </li>
    <li>
      If a parcel is refused or abandoned at customs, the outbound and return carriage
      come out of the refund.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Returns</h2>
  <p>
    Unopened, still-sealed product can be returned within <%= returnWindowDays %> days of
    delivery. If an item arrives damaged or is not what you ordered we pay the return
    postage and you choose between a replacement and a full refund<% if (freeReturns) { %>;
    if you simply changed your mind, we pay the return postage on that too<% } else { %>; for a change of
    mind the return postage is yours<% } %>. The full terms, including how to start a return,
    are on the <a href="<%= marketPath('/refund-policy') %>">Refund Policy</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions about a shipment</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:<%= b.supportEmail %>"><%= b.supportEmail %></a> with your order
    number, or use the <a href="<%= marketPath('/contact') %>">contact form</a>. We reply within
    <%= b.responseTimeHours %> hours, <%= b.supportHours ? b.supportHours.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + b.supportHours.slice(1) : 'on business days' %>.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  /* A printed document: overline, serif title over an ink rule, numbered
     sections at a ~65ch measure, the delivery table as a ruled ledger. */
  .ship-page { max-width: 56rem; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; counter-reset: shipsec; }
  .ship-page__title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.6vw, 3.3rem); font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.03; color: var(--color-ink); font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144; padding-bottom: 1.1rem; border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--color-ink); }
  .ship-page__lede { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 300; font-size: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-text); margin-top: 1.25rem; max-width: 60ch; font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 36; }
  .ship-page h2 { counter-increment: shipsec; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.9rem; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.55rem; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--color-ink); margin: 2.75rem 0 1rem; padding-bottom: 0.6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-light); }
  .ship-page h2::before { content: '\00A7\00A0' counter(shipsec, decimal-leading-zero); flex-shrink: 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--color-text-faint); }
  .ship-page > p { font-size: 0.96rem; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 1rem; max-width: 65ch; }
  .ship-page ul { list-style: none; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; padding: 0; max-width: 65ch; }
  .ship-page li { position: relative; padding-left: 1.4rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-text); margin-bottom: 0.55rem; }
  .ship-page li::before { content: '\2014'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-text-faint); }
  .ship-page strong { color: var(--color-ink); }
  .ship-page a { color: var(--color-primary); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }

  .legal-table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin: 0.25rem 0 1.1rem; }
  .ship-page .legal-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.88rem; min-width: 34rem; margin: 0; }
  .ship-page .legal-table th, .ship-page .legal-table td { text-align: left; padding: 0.72rem 0.9rem 0.72rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-light); }
  .ship-page .legal-table thead th { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 500; font-size: 0.66rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: var(--color-text-muted); border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--color-ink); background: transparent; }
  .ship-page .legal-table tbody th { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: inherit; font-weight: 500; text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0; color: var(--color-ink); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-light); }
  .ship-page .legal-table td { color: var(--color-text); }
  .ship-page .legal-table td:nth-child(3) { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .ship-free { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem !important; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-accent) !important; }

  /* The headline terms, set as a slip under an ink rule */
  .ship-banner { background: var(--color-bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--color-border-light); border-top: 1.5px solid var(--color-ink); border-radius: 0; padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 15rem) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1.5rem; align-items: baseline; }
  .ship-banner__head { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.45rem; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .ship-banner__sub { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.75; max-width: 60ch; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .ship-page__lede { font-size: 1.06rem; }
    .ship-banner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.15rem; }
    .ship-page h2 { font-size: 1.35rem; margin-top: 2.25rem; }
    .ship-page .legal-table { min-width: 0; font-size: 0.8rem; }
    .ship-page .legal-table th, .ship-page .legal-table td { padding: 0.6rem 0.5rem 0.6rem 0; }
    .ship-page .legal-table thead th { font-size: 0.58rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
    .ship-page .legal-table td:nth-child(3) { font-size: 0.72rem; }
    .ship-page .legal-table th:last-child, .ship-page .legal-table td:last-child { padding-right: 0; text-align: right; }
  }
</style>
